Focus solely on Reuters news wires for economic data releases and company announcements. If Reuters reports significant positive deviations from expected economic indicators (e.g., GDP growth, inflation), provide a positive sentiment. If Reuters reports negative surprises, provide a negative sentiment. Ignore expert opinions and commentary. Base your conviction on the magnitude of the deviation. A massive unexpected positive or negative shock to a market indicator such as a large negative jobs number should yield a high conviction score, even if some other sources provide conflicting evidence. A close result in a market number like CPI compared to estimates should mean a low conviction score.